{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-86-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "All acceptance criteria for INC-86 are satisfied, and the full test suite (`npm run check`) passes.\n\n**Fix:** `mustSegregate` in `src/cargo/hazmat.ts` was normalizing hazard classes with `primaryClass`, which strips the division (e.g. `\"5.1\"` → `\"5\"`). But the `SEGREGATION` table keys divisions like `\"5.1\"`, `\"5.2\"`, `\"2.1\"`, `\"4.1\"` in full, so any class with a division never matched — letting explosives sit next to oxidisers undetected. Changed the lookup to use the trimmed full class string instead of the stripped primary class.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9vvqPqgx8EQGa4FSGZ", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "a0f33ff2-530a-4a9b-b3da-74b1e790b338", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:49:12.998Z", "type": "assistant"}
